@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title PLANNED — ship the built work, then reach

component "**Now — ship what exists**" as NOW <<app>>
component "**Later — reach & polish**" as LATER <<app>>
component "**Horizon — isolation substrate**" as HZ <<cloud>>

NOW ARROW_MAIN LATER
LATER ARROW_OPTIONAL HZ

note right of NOW
  * ""mise deploy-cli"" — publish the CLI carrying the
    capability picker, cursor broker-default, local-model
    wiring, host-GPU / ""--gpus"" routing
  * ""mise deploy"" the images — ""base-node-browser"" and the
    ""-browser"" variants are unpublished
  * unblock the macOS keychain
    (""docker-credential-osxkeychain -50"") so registry
    push/pull auth works again
  //Outcome:// ""curl … | bash"" installs the current CLI and
  the browser variants are pullable.
end note

note right of LATER
  * **cursor under enforced egress** — decrypt
    cursor-agent's TLS to its backend so firewall can
    broker it, or document the broker-only limitation as
    permanent
  * ""PROVEO_EGRESS_INSPECTOR"" — attach the firewall
    inspector to any harness, reusing the sidecar / log /
    dashboard pipeline
  * publish the **egress-dashboard** build and smoke it
    against a recorded ""flows.ndjson""
  * record the live hero gif (""vhs _spec/_assets/hero.tape"")
    once the host toolchain is unbroken, replacing the
    hand-built asset
end note

note bottom of HZ
  Docker Sandboxes could collapse most of the bespoke
  isolation stack. The experiment is owned by Cursor's
  egress gap (pinned TLS + dead Landlock; free-tier local
  ""sbx policy"" — not AI Governance). claudecode's
  container story remains a secondary unlock versus DinD.
  Open questions (platform gating, the DLP content-scan
  gap, pre-GA status, and whether adoption reframes proveo
  as Kits on ""sbx"") are mapped in
  _spec/_experiments/docker-sandbox.puml
end note
@enduml
